[ ] Add or modify polars `drop_nans`. This interface was added to `LazyFrame` and `DataFrame` since 11/27/2024 (So late!). Seems that the old version we pinned do not have this yet.
    Updating the forked version might work.
    
    The official implementation:

    ```rs
    pub fn drop_nans(self, subset: Option<Vec<Expr>>) -> Self {
        if let Some(subset) = subset {
            self.filter(
                all_horizontal(
                    subset
                        .into_iter()
                        .map(|v| v.is_not_nan())
                        .collect::<Vec<_>>(),
                )
                .unwrap(),
            )
        } else {
            self.filter(
                // TODO: when Decimal supports NaN, include here
                all_horizontal([dtype_cols([DataType::Float32, DataType::Float64]).is_not_nan()])
                    .unwrap(),
            )
        }
    }
    ```


